This file stands in for SFA2223_Dict.zip -> sfa2223.xlsx on bin/fetch-ipeds'
offline (-F) route, the way the *-fixture.csv files stand in for the survey
CSVs. It is deliberately NOT a real .xlsx: the fetcher decides zip-ness by
reading the payload, so a real workbook here would be opened as an archive and
its own XML parts searched for a member. Nothing reads these bytes -- the
dictionary is pinned for its digest and for the citation behind
IpedsImputationFlag, and the ingest never opens it.

The real dictionary's "imputation values" sheet is the published list of the
thirteen X codes:

  A Not applicable                         B Institution left item blank
  C Analyst corrected reported value       D Do not know
  G Data generated from other data values  H Value not derived - data not usable
  J Logical imputation                     K Ratio adjustment
  L Imputed using the Group Median         N Imputed using Nearest Neighbor
  P Imputed using Carry Forward            R Reported
  Z Implied zero;
